    "summary_en": "China Vanke's 2024 annual report shows operating revenue of 343.18 billion yuan, down 26.32% year on year, and a net loss attributable to shareholders of 49.48 billion yuan, versus a profit of 12.16 billion yuan in 2023. Basic loss per share was 4.17 yuan. The board proposed no cash dividend, no bonus share issue and no capitalisation of reserves for 2024, subject to shareholder meeting approval. Total assets fell to 1,286.26 billion yuan and net assets attributable to shareholders fell to 202.67 billion yuan, with an asset-liability ratio of 73.66%. The shareholder letter acknowledges liquidity pressure and states the company is managing risks and restructuring its financing model.",
